    "conventions": "Filipinos carry a given name (often two, like John Paul or Mary Grace), the mother's maiden family name as a middle name, and the father's family name last: Maria Cruz Santos. Most family names are Spanish, handed out from a catalogue in 1849, so Santos, Reyes and Cruz are everywhere. Almost everyone also has a nickname that friends use instead (Jun, Bong, Tin, Ging). Chinese Filipinos (Tsinoy) often carry short Hokkien family names such as Tan, Sy, Go and Uy.",
